    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_001", "Traveler's Bow", "A small bow used by travelers for protection.\nIt doesn't do a lot of damage, but it can be\nused to attack foes from a distance."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_002", "Soldier’s Bow", "A bow designed for armed conflict.\nInflicts more damage than a civilian bow,\nbut it will still burn if it touches fire."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_003", "Spiked Boko Bow", "An upgraded Boko bow bound with animal\nbone to boost its durability and firepower.\nIts craftsmanship is sloppy, but it's light and\neasy to use."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_004", "Boko Bow", "A basic Bokoblin bow made of wood. It's\nmade by taking any tree branch and just\ntying a string to either end, so don't expect\nmuch in the way of combat effectiveness."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_006", "Lizal Bow", "A wooden bow created by Lizalfos. It's\nreinforced by the bones of a large fish—\na marked improvement over any standard\nwooden bow."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_009", "Lynel Bow", "A Lynel-made bow crafted from rough metal.\nTrue to the vicious nature of Lynel weaponry,\nit fires a spread of multiple arrows at once.\nIdeal for taking down quick-moving targets."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_011", "Strengthened Lizal Bow", "A Lizal bow with a grip reinforced by metal.\nThe body is made from the branches of a\nflexible tree that grows near water, which\noffers some serious destructive power."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_013", "Forest Dweller's Bow", "The Koroks made this bow for Hylians. It's\ncrafted from flexible wood and uses sturdy\nvines for the bowstring. Its construction may\nbe simple, but it fires multiple arrows at once."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_014", "Silver Bow", "A bow favored by the Zora for fishing.\nIt doesn't boast the highest firepower,\nbut the special metal it's crafted from\nprioritizes durability."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_015", "Golden Bow", "This Gerudo-made bow is popular for the fine\nornamentations along its limbs. Designed for\nhunting and warfare alike, this bow was\nengineered to strike distant targets."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_016", "Swallow Bow", "This bow is a favorite among Rito warriors.\nThe bowstring has been specially engineered\nfor aerial combat, which allows it to be drawn\nfaster than a normal bow."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_017", "Falcon Bow", "A highly refined Rito-made bow created by\na master Rito craftsman. Rito warriors favor\nit for its superior rate of fire, which helps\nthem excel even further at aerial combat."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_023", "Ancient Bow", "This bow is the result of Robbie's research.\nAncient Sheikah technology affords it\nheightened functionality. Arrows fired from\nit travel in a perfectly straight line."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_026", "Mighty Lynel Bow", "This massive Lynel bow sports a bowstring\nmade from a metal so tough, mere Hylians\nhave trouble drawing it back."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_027", "Dragon Bone Boko Bow", "A Boko bow reinforced by fossils. Bokoblins\nhandpicked the materials it's made from, so\nit boasts a respectable firepower."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_028", "Great Eagle Bow", "A bow without equal wielded by the Rito\nChampion, Revali. It's said Revali could loose\narrows with the speed of a gale, making him\nsupreme in aerial combat."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_029", "Phrenic Bow", "A bow passed down through the Sheikah\ntribe. Concentrating before drawing the\nstring will allow you to target distant\nenemies as easily as those nearby."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_030", "Steel Lizal Bow", "This bow is wielded by Lizalfos who are\nexpert marksmen. The metal that reinforces\nmuch of the weapon adds some additional\nweight but offers heightened durability."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_032", "Savage Lynel Bow", "This Lynel bow is made from a special steel\nfound at the peak of Death Mountain.\nIt has tremendous stopping power and can\npierce thick armor as easily as thin paper."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_033", "Royal Guard's Bow", "This prototype Sheikah-made bow was\ndesigned to fight the Great Calamity. Made\nwith ancient technology, it boasts a high rate\nof fire and firepower but has low durability."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_035", "Knight's Bow", "The sturdy metal construction of this bow\noffers superior durability, while its lack of\nfiring quirks makes it quite reliable. Once\nfavored by the knights at Hyrule Castle."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_036", "Royal Bow", "In the past, the king of Hyrule presented this\nbow to only the most talented archers in the\nland. Its combat capabilities are as\nimpressive as its extravagant design."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_038", "Wooden Bow", "This wooden bow may not be the most\nreliable for battling monsters, but it is\nexcellent for hunting small animals."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_040", "Duplex Bow", "A bow favored by the skilled archers of the\nYiga Clan. It's been engineered to fire two\narrows at once to ensure your target comes\nto a swift and none-too-pleasant halt."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_071", "Bow of Light", "Princess Zelda gave you this bow and arrow\nfor the battle with Dark Beast Ganon. When\nwielded by the hero, it fires arrows of pure\nlight strong enough to oppose the Calamity."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Bow_072", "Twilight Bow", "A bow used by the princess who fought the\nbeasts of twilight alongside the hero. It's said\nto contain the spirits of light's power. It fires\narrows straight and true, as if beams of light."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_001", "Traveler's Claymore", "A basic two-handed sword often\nwielded by aspiring adventurers.\nIts immense weight can knock enemies'\nshields right out of their hands."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_002", "Soldier's Claymore", "A two-handed sword designed for combat.\nIt's heavy and hard to use but has decent\nbuild quality and durability."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_003", "Knight's Claymore", "Only the most confident of Hyrule Castle's\nknights carried this two-handed sword. Its\ncutting edge is finely honed."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_004", "Boko Bat", "A clunky club made by a Bokoblin. If you\nswing it at an enemy's shield, it may be\nable to knock the shield out of your\nfoe's hand."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_005", "Spiked Boko Bat", "After much consideration by Bokoblins on\nhow to improve the Boko bat, they simply\nattached sharp spikes to it. A skilled fighter\ncan cause immense damage with this."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_006", "Dragonbone Boko Bat", "Used by only the toughest Bokoblin warriors,\nthis Boko bat has been fortified by fossilized\nbone. It boasts a high durability and is strong\nenough to beat down powerful foes."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_010", "Moblin Club", "A crudely fashioned club favored by Moblins.\nIt's carved from a sturdy tree but is sloppily\nmade, so it breaks easily."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_011", "Spiked Moblin Club", "Animal bone has been affixed to this\nMoblin club to greatly improve its damage."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_012", "Dragonbone Moblin Club", "The bone of an ancient beast has been\naffixed to this Moblin club, further increasing\nits damage. Moblins carrying these in battle\nare particularly dangerous."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_013", "Ancient Battle Axe", "A weapon used by Guardian Scouts.\nIts unique blade was forged using ancient\ntechnology. Although powerful, its unusual\nshape causes it to break easily."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_014", "Ancient Battle Axe+", "This ancient battle axe's damage output\nhas been increased to maximum. It's sharp\nenough to cut through almost anything, so\nit may have been used to forge new routes."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_015", "Ancient Battle Axe++", "This ancient battle axe's damage output is\nscaled up to peak performance. Ancient\ntechnology makes it possible to enhance\ncutting power beyond metal weapons' limits."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_016", "Lynel Crusher", "This two-handed weapon is favored by the\nLynels. It may be more accurate to call it a\nlump of metal than a weapon, but if wielded\nby a Lynel, it can pound you into a fine dust."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_017", "Mighty Lynel Crusher", "This Lynel-made two-handed weapon has\nbeen reinforced to increase its durability\nand striking power. Its overwhelming heft\nwill crush your foe, shield and all."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_018", "Savage Lynel Crusher", "This Lynel-made two-handed weapon is\nimmensely heavy thanks to a rare metal\nfrom Death Mountain's peak. The power of\nits downward swing is in a class all its own."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_019", "Moblin Arm", "A Moblin bone that continues to move even\nafter being detached from its body. The bone\nis thick enough to be used as a weapon but\nis extremely brittle and easily broken."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_020", "Rusty Claymore", "A two-handed sword not properly cared for.\nAlthough it can be used as a weapon, its\ndurability is very low. Don't expect it to\nlast for more than a few strikes."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_023", "Ancient Bladesaw", "This two-handed sword was forged using\nancient Sheikah technology. Its unique\nrotating blades give it impressive cutting\npower that will slice enemies to shreds."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_024", "Royal Claymore", "A two-handed sword issued to the Hyrulean\nroyal family's immediate guard detail.\nIts powerful strikes are said to crush an\nopponent's body and resolve alike."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_027", "Silver Longsword", "Although the Zora prefer spears to swords,\nthey made this two-handed weapon using\na special metal. It found popularity among\nHylians for its unique design."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_029", "Golden Claymore", "Only the most talented Gerudo sword fighters\ncarry this two-handed sword. It's actually\nmuch lighter than it appears and is\nsurprisingly easy to wield."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_030", "Double Axe", "This double-sided axe was designed with\nfighting in mind. It's a bit unwieldy, so it\nrequires a well-practiced technique to\nuse efficiently."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_031", "Iron Sledgehammer", "This large iron sledgehammer was originally\nused for mining, but it works reasonably well\nas a weapon too. "},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_032", "Woodcutter's Axe", "A woodcutter's tool of choice for felling trees.\nIts formidable weight and uneven balancing\nmake it a slow, inefficient weapon."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_033", "Great Flameblade", "This magic-infused greatsword was forged\nin the fires of Death Mountain by Goron\nsmiths in an ancient age. Attack when the\nblade glows red to expel flames."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_034", "Great Frostblade", "This magic-infused greatsword was forged\nby smelting ore found in the Hebra\nMountains' permafrost. Attack when the\nblade glows blue to expel freezing air."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_035", "Great Thunderblade", "This magic-infused greatsword was forged\nby the Hyrulean royal family using lightning\nfrom the Hyrule Hills. Attack when the blade\nglows golden to expel lightning."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_036", "Cobble Crusher", "A Goron-made two-handed weapon. It's\nmade from thick, hard metal and has no\ncutting edge, so it relies on its sheer\nweight to crush all opponents."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_037", "Stone Smasher", "A two-handed weapon forged from a rare\nmetal mined in Goron City. Its center of\ngravity is at its tip, so it uses centrifugal force\nand its sheer weight to smash opponents flat."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_038", "Boat Oar", "Made for paddling boats, but it was made\nsturdy enough to fight strong currents.\nMaybe it's useful for self-defense in a pinch."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_041", "Eightfold Longblade", "A single-edged sword seldom seen in Hyrule.\nThis weapon is passed down through the\nSheikah tribe and has an astonishingly\nsharp edge ideal for slicing."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_045", "Farming Hoe", "A farming tool primarily used for tilling fields.\nIts fine craftsmanship is sturdy enough\nto withstand backbreaking fieldwork, but\nits battle applications are untested."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_047", "Royal Guard's Claymore", "The Sheikah used the very essence of\nancient technology to forge this greatsword.\nIt was designed to oppose the Calamity, but\nits low durability made it impractical in battle."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_051", "Giant Boomerang", "This massive boomerang requires two hands.\nOriginally used for hunting, it was modified\nfor use as a weapon. The blades on the\ninner curves make it a bit tricky to wield."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_054", "Boulder Breaker", "This two-handed weapon was once wielded\nby the Goron Champion Daruk. Daruk made\nswinging it around look easy, but a Hylian\nwould need an immense amount of strength."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_055", "Edge of Duality", "A curious double-edged sword crafted using\nSheikah technology. It was originally made\nfor Hyrulean knights unfamiliar with single-\nedged blades."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_056", "Korok Leaf", "A single swing of this giant, sturdy leaf can\ncreate a gust of wind strong enough to blow\naway light objects. These will sometimes fall\noff trees as they're chopped down."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_057", "Sword of the Six Sages", "The Six Sages are said to have forged this\nlongsword to seal a demon king in the world\nwhere the hero fought against the beasts of\ntwilight. The blade shines with a holy luster."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_059", "Biggoron's Sword", "A legendary greatsword forged by a Goron\ncraftsman for a hero who traveled through\ntime. The exceptionally sharp cutting edge\nis a testament to the craftsman's mastery."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_060", "Fierce Deity Sword", "A peculiar greatsword allegedly used by a\nhero from a world in which the moon\nthreatened to fall. It slashes wildly in battle\nas if possessed by a fierce deity."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Lsword_074", "Windcleaver", "This sword is favored by high-ranking\nmembers of the Yiga. When wielded by a\nproficient fighter, its unique shape cleaves\nthe very wind and creates a vacuum."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_001", "Wooden Shield", "This lightweight, simple shield is ideal for\nless-experienced fighters. It can withstand\nlight attacks, but blocking stronger blows\nis not recommended."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_002", "Soldier’s Shield", "A shield once used by the guards of Hyrule\nCastle. It's easy to handle, but its core is \nmade of wood, so it can catch fire."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_003", "Knight's Shield", "A shield favored by the knights who served\nthe Hyrulean royal family. Its sturdy metal\nconstruction makes it quite durable, but\nits weight requires decent skill to wield."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_004", "Boko Shield", "A Bokoblin-made shield created by attaching\na handhold to any flat tree bark picked up\noff the ground. It's pretty shoddy, so don't\nexpect it to last very long."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_005", "Spiked Boko Shield", "A Boko shield made of slightly stronger\nwood and reinforced with animal bones."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_006", "Dragonbone Boko Shield", "This Boko shield is reinforced with fossilized\nbone. Its defensive capabilities are\nrespectable, but its predictably slipshod\ncraftsmanship spells low durability."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_007", "Lizal Shield", "A common shield found among the Lizalfos.\nIt's made of metal, but its sloppy\ncraftsmanship offers poor durability."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_008", "Reinforced Lizal Shield", "This Lizal shield has been strengthened by\nadding a different type of metal to the mix.\nThe edge is lined with spikes, so handle\nwith care."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_009", "Steel Lizal Shield", "This Lizal shield is adorned with several\nmetal shells as a means of reinforcement.\nIts defensive capabilities are high, but its\nweight requires a skilled soldier to bear."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_013", "Guardian Shield", "A shield made with ancient Sheikah\ntechnology. It can deflect a Guardian\nScout's beam."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_014", "Guardian Shield+", "This larger version of a Guardian shield\nhas had its output level boosted. Its\ndefensive capabilities are comparable to\nthose of a metal shield's."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_015", "Guardian Shield++", "The output level of this shield has been\nboosted to maximum. Its combat capabilities\nsurpass those of metallic shields, and it\ncan deflect Guardian Scout beams."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_016", "Lynel Shield", "A sturdy shield favored by Lynels for its\ndefensive and offensive capabilities. First\nand foremost a shield, but the bladed edges\ncan deal slashing attacks when deflecting."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_017", "Mighty Lynel Shield", "This Lynel-made shield has been reinforced\nwith armor and even more blades. Stronger\nin both defense and offense, it can tear\nthrough basic armor when deflecting."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_018", "Savage Lynel Shield", "This ultimate Lynel shield is used only by the\nwhite-haired Lynels. It excels at defending\nagainst even the most brutal of attacks and\ncutting down powerful foes when deflecting."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_021", "Rusty Shield", "It's likely this rusty old shield once belonged\nto a knight. It still has some defensive\ncapabilities, but its usefulness has been\nworn down by time."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_022", "Royal Shield", "A shield issued to the Hyrulean royal\nfamily's immediate guard detail. It boasts a\nhigh defense, but these days it's more a\ncollector's item due to its ornamentation."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_023", "Forest Dweller's Shield", "The Koroks made this shield specifically for\nHylians. It's made from the finest hard wood\nof trees that grow only in the Korok forest, so\nit's sturdier than it looks."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_025", "Silver Shield", "A Zora-made shield adorned with intricate\nornamentation. It's said that true masters\nof this shield can redirect attacks as a rock\nredirects rushing water."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_026", "Gerudo Shield", "The design of this metal shield has changed\nover time to match the Gerudo's sword-and-\nshield fighting style. It's favored by soldiers\nand travelers alike."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_030", "Hylian Shield", "A shield passed down through the Hyrulean\nroyal family, along with the legend of the\nhero who wielded it. Its defensive capabilities\nand durability outshine all other shields."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_031", "Hunter's Shield", "Favored by hunters for its rabbit design,\nwhich is said to bring luck on hunts. It's\neasy to use, but its durability leaves\nsomething to be desired."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_032", "Fisherman's Shield", "Often carried by fishermen for its fish design,\nwhich represents hope for a great catch. Its\nlight wooden construction makes it\nconvenient to take onto a boat."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_033", "Royal Guard's Shield", "This shield was forged using ancient Sheikah\ntechnology. It boasts extremely high stopping\npower, but its structural weakness made its\nlow durability impractical for combat."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_034", "Emblazoned Shield", "This shield features a traditional design from\nNecluda. Its combat capabilities aren't much\nbetter than the standard wooden shield, but\nit found popularity for its design."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_035", "Traveler's Shield", "A sturdy shield loved by many an adventurer.\nIt is made of animal hide and sturdy wood\nand is best suited to defending against weak\nmonsters or animals."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_036", "Radiant Shield", "This extravagant shield is presented to\nGerudo warriors who rise to the rank of\ncaptain. Its apparent opulence is rivaled\nonly by its combat capabilities."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_037", "Daybreaker", "This shield was cherished by the Gerudo\nChampion Urbosa. The gold used to make it\nwas handpicked to ensure a design that is\nboth lightweight and very durable."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_038", "Ancient Shield", "This shield was made using ancient Sheikah\ntechnology. Its surface glows blue when\nraised in defense. Enhanced functionality\nallows it to deflect Guardian beams."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_040", "Pot Lid", "The lid of a large soup pot. It smells vaguely\nof poultry broth... Yum! It can take quite a\nbeating before breaking."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_041", "Shield of the Mind's Eye", "A small Sheikah-made shield. Its design is\nintended to decrease blind spots without\nsacrificing too much defense."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_042", "Kite Shield", "Rito warriors cherish this shield. Its unique\nshape is designed with mid-battle flight in\nmind to facilitate aerial combat."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Shield_057", "Hero's Shield", "A shield said to have been the favorite of a\nhero who traveled the open seas. It was\napparently a family heirloom, passed down\nthrough many generations."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_001", "Traveler's Spear", "A spear used mainly by travelers to fend off\nwolves and other beasts. It's easy to hold\nand simple to use."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_002", "Soldier's Spear", "A long spear once used by the guards of\nHyrule Castle. Easy to use but difficult to\nmaster. The iron tip is very sturdy, and the\nshaft will not burn when exposed to flame."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_003", "Knight's Halberd", "A spear used by knights adept in mounted\ncombat. The spearhead is modeled after\nan axe."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_004", "Boko Spear", "A spear haphazardly carved from a large tree\nbranch. It looks like its original intent was for\nskewering meat and cooking it, but it does\nhave some combat merit as well."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_005", "Spiked Boko Spear", "A Boko spear enhanced with sharpened\nanimal bones. It's light, easy to use, and\ndeals a decent amount of damage."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_006", "Dragonbone Boko Spear", "This Boko spear has been strengthened with\nfossilized bones. The bones are positioned\noutward so the fangs bite at the opponent.\nBeware Bokoblins carrying this weapon."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_007", "Lizal Spear", "The brutal, ripping edge of this weapon's\nspearhead is a distinctly Lizalfos design.\nIts low durability doesn't lend itself to\nextended use."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_008", "Enhanced Lizal Spear", "Judging by the harpoon-like spearhead of\nthis Lizalfos-made spear, the Lizalfos use\nit for fishing as well as combat. Try not to\nget caught on the wrong end of its barbs."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_009", "Forked Lizal Spear", "Skilled Lizalfos warriors tend to favor this\nspear. What it lacks in piercing power, it\nmakes up for with the brutal wounds its\ndual ripping blades will inflict."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_010", "Moblin Spear", "This wooden spear is most often used by\nMoblins. It's made from a hastily whittled\ntree, so its stabbing power and durability\nare both pretty low."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_011", "Spiked Moblin Spear", "This Moblin-made spear uses a horned\nanimal bone as the spearhead. Like many\nMoblin weapons it's sloppily made, but this\none packs some respectable piercing power."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_012", "Dragonbone Moblin Spear", "This spear is a fan favorite among Moblins.\nThe spearhead is made from fossilized\nbones adorned with spikes, which greatly\nincreases its stabbing power."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_013", "Guardian Spear", "Wielded by Guardian Scouts, this spear has\na high piercing power and is a testament to\nthe Sheikah's high level of technology. The\nspearhead appears only when brandished."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_014", "Guardian Spear+", "The tip of this Guardian spear has been\nenlarged and strengthened. It's a bit shorter\nthan your average spear, perhaps to facilitate\nuse in tight spaces."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_015", "Guardian Spear++", "This Guardian spear's output has been\nboosted to the maximum. The spearhead\nis designed for optimal stabbing, capable\nof easily piercing most armor."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_016", "Lynel Spear", "The crescent-shaped spearhead of this\nLynel-made weapon gives it poor balance,\nmaking it difficult to wield. Lynels, however,\ncan swing it effectively with a single hand."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_017", "Mighty Lynel Spear", "The weight and cutting edge of this Lynel-\nmade spear have both been enhanced. It's\nimmensely heavy for a Hylian, but a Lynel\ncan cleave through rock with a single swing."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_018", "Savage Lynel Spear", "White-haired Lynels favor this brutal spear.\nIts axe-like spearhead and exceptional \nweight give it absolute destructive power."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_021", "Rusty Halberd", "A rusty polearm likely used by knights from\nan age past. The spearhead is in bad shape\ndue to prolonged exposure to the elements,\nso its durability is low."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_022", "Farmer's Pitchfork", "A farming tool used to collect hay efficiently.\nIt's light enough to be used by anyone.\nThe four prongs are very sharp."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_023", "Ancient Spear", "This spear is the result of countless hours\nof research into the ancient technology\nused by Guardians. The glowing spearhead\nhas high piercing potential."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_024", "Royal Halberd", "This spear was issued to the knights who\nguarded Hyrule Castle's throne room. Its\nornate design was applied by a craftsman\nin service to the royal family."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_025", "Forest Dweller's Spear", "The Koroks made this spear for Hylians.\nThe shaft is made from a light, sturdy wood,\noffering ease of use. The spearhead is made\nfrom a much harder wood, offering strength."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_027", "Zora Spear", "This spear is a Zora's weapon of choice.\nIt's lighter than it looks due to being made\nfrom a special metal and is used by the Zora\nfor both fishing and protecting their domain."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_028", "Silverscale Spear", "The most skilled Zora fighters wield this\nspear. Its beautiful fish-tail design belies\nits impressive strength; the spearhead\ncan pierce even the toughest scales."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_029", "Gerudo Spear", "This spear's center of gravity is in its tip,\nmaking it a bit unwieldy for the average\nfighter. But in the hands of a skilled Gerudo\nwarrior, it's a weapon of reliable strength."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_030", "Throwing Spear", "A specialized spear weighted to excel as a\nthrowing weapon. It's perfectly balanced\nto be thrown farther than your average spear,\nable to pierce targets from a great distance."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_031", "Drillshaft", "Goron artisans used recycled metal to forge\nthis weapon. The tip is made from an old\nexcavation bore, which affords it unmatched\npiercing capabilities."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_032", "Feathered Spear", "Its lightweight design is a hallmark of\nRito craftsmanship. It's made from light\nand sturdy materials, which afford Rito\nwarriors ease of use during aerial combat."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_033", "Flamespear", "A magical spear forged in the magma of\nDeath Mountain. Attack when the blade\nglows to expel powerful flames."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_034", "Frostspear", "A magical spear forged from ancient ice\ntaken from the Hebra Mountains. Attack\nwhen the blade glows blue to chill the air\nand freeze your foe."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_035", "Thunderspear", "A magical spear that contains thunder from\nThundra Plateau in its tip. Attack when the\nblade glows with a golden light to unleash\nan electrical attack."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_036", "Wooden Mop", "Just a mop to the untrained eye, it excels at\ntidying up the place. But it owes its sturdy\nconstruction to a true craftsman, so it\nactually has some combat merit."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_037", "Serpentine Spear", "The spearhead of this weapon is uniquely\nSheikah in design. Spear masters of the\nSheikah tribe can use the crescent shape to\nsnag their opponents and deliver brutal cuts."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_038", "Fishing Harpoon", "A fisherman's tool that excels at catching\nlarge fish. Its particularly sharp spearhead\nmakes it valuable as a weapon as well."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_047", "Royal Guard's Spear", "This Sheikah-made spear was created using\nancient technology to combat the Calamity.\nIts attack power is very high, but a critical\ndesign flaw left it with poor durability."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_049", "Ceremonial Trident", "A spear modeled after the Lightscale Trident\nwielded by the Zora Champion Mipha. They\nmay be identical in appearance, but this\nspear's strength and durability are inferior."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Spear_050", "Lightscale Trident", "A spear of peerless grace cherished by the\nZora Champion Mipha. Although Mipha\nspecialized in healing abilities, her\nspearmanship was in a class all its own."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_001", "Traveler's Sword", "A very common sword often kept by travelers\nto fend off small beasts. It's fairly durable\nbut a bit unreliable against monsters."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_002", "Soldier's Broadsword", "A sword brandished by the soldiers who\nonce protected Hyrule Castle. Its durable\nblade is well tuned for slaying monsters."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_003", "Knight's Broadsword", "Knights of Hyrule once carried this sword.\nThese days it's the weapon of choice for\nseasoned adventurers thanks to its ease\nof use and high attack power."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_004", "Boko Club", "A crude Bokoblin club made to clobber small\nprey. It's essentially a stick, so its durability\nis low."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_005", "Spiked Boko Club", "A reinforced Bokoblin club made to maximize\ndamage. The sharpened bones jabbed into it\nmake it a brutal weapon."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_006", "Dragonbone Boko Club", "This Bokoblin club has been reinforced with\nfossilized bones to maximize clobbering\npotential. Only the brawniest of Bokoblins\ncan manage its immense weight."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_007", "Lizal Boomerang", "A curved sword favored by the Lizalfos.\nIt can be used to attack directly or can\nbe thrown like a boomerang."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_008", "Lizal Forked Boomerang", "Blue Lizalfos in particular like this weapon.\nIt has one more blade than the\nLizal boomerang to give it additional cutting\npower, and it still returns when thrown."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_009", "Lizal Tri-Boomerang", "More blades means more attack power!\nIt can be used as a boomerang, but all those\nblades makes that a bit more dangerous.\nCarried by Black Lizalfos seasoned in battle."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_013", "Guardian Sword", "A sword often wielded by Guardian Scouts.\nIts blue energy blade is a product of ancient\ntechnology. It's not very durable."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_014", "Guardian Sword+", "This Guardian sword has enhanced power\nover the standard model. Its cutting\ncapabilities are improved, and its durability\nhas seen a slight uptick."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_015", "Guardian Sword++", "The abilities of this Guardian sword have\nbeen boosted to the maximum, as evidenced\nby its increase in size. It slices through\narmor like a hot knife through butter!"},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_016", "Lynel Sword", "This Lynel-made sword was designed with\nsmashing in mind rather than slicing. It's\non the heavy side compared to what Hylians\nare used to, but it's very strong."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_017", "Mighty Lynel Sword", "This Lynel-made sword boasts more blades\nand more attack power. A skilled Lynel can\ndraw this sword simply in passing and still\ncut a foe in two."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_018", "Savage Lynel Sword", "A brutal sword carried by white-haired\nLynels. The savage blades are strong\nenough to cut down any foe, no matter how\nstrong."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_019", "Bokoblin Arm", "A skeletal arm that keeps moving even after\nit’s severed from its body. It's kind of gross to\nstrap it to your back, but it'll do in a pinch.\nIt's old and fragile, so it's quick to break."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_020", "Lizalfos Arm", "The arm of a Stalizalfos that continues to\nstruggle even in death. It can be used as a\nweapon, but it's very brittle. You can feel it\nwiggling when you strap it to your back..."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_021", "Rusty Broadsword", "This once-fearsome sword has seen better\ndays. It can do some damage in the right\nhands but also breaks quickly."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_022", "Soup Ladle", "A kitchen implement often used for serving\ndelicious soups. It was carved from the wood\nof a sturdy tree, so it actually packs quite\nthe wallop."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_023", "Ancient Short Sword", "The blade of this sword was made using an\nancient power lost to this modern age. Its\nblade appears only when drawn, and its\ncutting power surpasses metal swords."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_024", "Royal Broadsword", "The Hyrulean royal family would award this\nsword to knights who achieved remarkable\nfeats. A sword that balances strength and\nbeauty as elegantly as this one is a rare find."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_025", "Forest Dweller's Sword", "Koroks made this sword for Hylians. It's\nmade of wood, so it isn't the best choice for\nhead-on attacks. Its original intent was likely\nclearing vines to forge paths through forests."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_027", "Zora Sword", "The ornamentation that adorns this blade is\na traditional Zora design. It's forged from a\nvery durable and rust-proof metal."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_029", "Gerudo Scimitar", "This common sword is often carried by\nGerudo women for self-defense. Its short,\ncurved blade is easily recognized."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_030", "Moonlight Scimitar", "Delicate Gerudo carvings decorate this\ncurved sword. The engraved blade is\nextremely sharp. Apparently it once\nserved ceremonial purposes in festivals."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_031", "Feathered Edge", "Rito craftsmen forged this lightweight,\ndouble-edged sword so Rito warriors\ncould soar into battle unhindered by\nits weight."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_033", "Flameblade", "This magical sword was forged in the lava\nof Death Mountain. It leaves white-hot flames\nin its wake when the blade glows red."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_034", "Frostblade", "A magical sword forged in the frigid\nmountains of the Hebra region. When\nthe blade glows blue, enemies struck\nby it will become frozen."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_035", "Thunderblade", "A magical sword forged and refined by\nlightning from the Hyrule Hills. When the\nblade shines with a golden light, it will\nelectrocute enemies struck by it."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_040", "Spring-Loaded Hammer", "This strange hammer is one of Kilton's\nspecialties. Being struck by it doesn't hurt\nmuch, but the fourth swing in a string of\nattacks will send the victim flying."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_041", "Eightfold Blade", "A single-edged sword traditional to the\nSheikah tribe. Forged using ancient\ntechnology, it just may be among the\nsharpest conventional weapons ever made."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_043", "Torch", "This torch will stay lit once ignited, but if you\nput it away, the flame will be extinguished\nuntil you light it again."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_044", "Tree Branch", "Wooden branches such as this are pretty\ncommon, but it's surprisingly well-balanced.\nIt doesn't do much damage but can serve\nas a weapon in a pinch."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_047", "Royal Guard's Sword", "A Sheikah-made replica of the sword that\nseals the darkness. It was made with ancient\ntechnology to oppose the Great Calamity,\nbut its low durability made it inefficient."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_048", "Meteor Rod", "A magical rod that can cast three fireballs\nat once, crafted by an ancient magician.\nIt will break upon running out of magical\nenergy, so make it last!"},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_049", "Blizzard Rod", "A magical rod that can cast extreme cold in\na wide range. These are crafted from refined\nice found at the summit of Hebra Peak.\nIt will break when depleted."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_050", "Thunderstorm Rod", "A magical rod that can hurl three balls of\nelectricity at once. Its gem contains\nelectricity from the Hyrule Hills, and the rod\nwill break when that electricity runs out."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_051", "Boomerang", "This throwing weapon was originally used by\nthe forest-dwelling Koroks. Its unique shape\nallows it to return after being thrown."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_052", "Scimitar of the Seven", "A famous sword once beloved by the Gerudo\nChampion Urbosa. It is said that when\nUrbosa swung this sword in battle, her\nmovements resembled a beautiful dance."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_053", "Vicious Sickle", "A grim weapon favored by the Yiga. The half-\nmoon shape of the blade allows for the rapid\ndelivery of fatal wounds and serves as a\nsymbol of their terror. Its durability is low."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_057", "Goddess Sword", "A sword said to have once belonged to a\nhero from the sky. Its blade houses the fire\nof the Goddess. When wielded, a strange\nyet heavenly breeze kicks up around you."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_058", "Sword", "A sword once wielded by a hero in an\nancient age. When grasped, a strange sense\nof nostalgia washes over you. Take it when\ngoing alone would otherwise be dangerous."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_059", "Sea-Breeze Boomerang", "A boomerang said to have been used by a\nhero who traveled the Great Sea. It smells\nfaintly of salt water."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_060", "Fire Rod", "A magical rod that can cast fireballs, crafted\nby an ancient magician. The rod will break if\nit strikes something directly, so use it wisely."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_061", "Ice Rod", "A magical rod crafted from refined ice found\nin the Hebra Mountains. This rod can cast\nwaves of freezing air. Great for magic—not so\ngreat for melee."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_062", "Lightning Rod", "A magical rod that can shoot balls of\nelectricity. Its gem contains lightning from\nthe Hyrule Hills. It's not recommended to\nuse as a melee weapon."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_070", "Master Sword", "The legendary sword that seals the\ndarkness. Its blade gleams with a sacred\nluster that can oppose the Calamity. Only a\nhero chosen by the sword itself may wield it."},
    ItemText{"Weapon_Sword_073", "Demon Carver", "This lethal weapon is forged by the Yiga.\nIts unique shape facilitates the sound\ndispatching of any target and strikes\nfear into the hearts of all who see it."},
